# markdown.view: markdown drawn to the width it is given, a split's prose side first of all.
#
#   @{view:split}
#   ```mermaid
#   flowchart TD
#       A[source] --> B[render]
#   ```
#   ```markdown
#   ## What it shows
#   - the message leaves **raw**
#   - the hook draws it again
#   ```
#
# A bare ```markdown fence under a split takes this view, as a bare quote takes quote.view.
# @{view:markdown} over the same fence draws it alone, at the terminal's width.
#
# @markdown hands the body its source DRAWN (src/markdown.ts): headings bold, lists and
# quotes hanging from their marker, rules across the width, code indented, paragraphs
# folded. A body holding a code fence of its own opens under a longer run, ````markdown.
#
# Where this hook does not run, the fence shows as the code block it is: the source, legible
# as written.
@markdown
${content}
